I fixed this by adding Gson keep rules to `app/proguard-rules.pro`. I couldn't build or run the app here, so this is verified by reading the code only.

**Cause:** The release build sets `isMinifyEnabled = true` (in `app/build.gradle.kts`), and the project's ProGuard rules file was empty. R8 removed the generic signature from the anonymous `object : TypeToken<List<Book>>() {}` in `CatalogRepository.kt`, so Gson saw no type argument and threw.

**Change:** The rules file now:
- keeps `Signature`, annotation, `EnclosingMethod`, and `InnerClasses` attributes, which Gson needs at runtime;
- keeps `TypeToken` and every subclass of it, with `allowobfuscation` so R8 can still rename them;
- keeps all classes in `vn.shelftap.lab.model` so `Book`'s fields survive shrinking;
- suppresses a `sun.misc.**` warning that Gson commonly triggers.

I assumed `Book` lives in `vn.shelftap.lab.model`, based on the import in `CatalogRepository.kt`. I didn't open that file. If you later rename or move the model package, update the `-keep` line to match.

The debug build doesn't minify, which is why the error appears only in release builds.
